    "turn_text": "I treat each issue as it comes along. I strongly support what the president's doing with MS-13. I strongly support what he's done with ISIS. And overall, the national economy is probably the best it's been in more than a generation. But no, in Russia, he was clearly wrong. There was no doubt at all that Russia did interfere in our election. Now, the president can't make the distinction. To me, there is no evidence at all that there was any collusion between the Trump campaign and Russia. That, to me, is wrong with this investigation. has gone on to that extent, because it was more like a teleknife, than there for more than 60, 65 witnesses. There's no evidence at all of any collusion. But the president can't make the distinction. There's not only evidence, it actually concludes a proof that Russia interfered in the last election. They started interfering before Donald Trump even became an candidate. They are constantly interfering in our country. They're constantly trying to hack into our defense secrets, to our private sector. Russia is an aggressive nation. And the irony in all this, though, the president refused to condemn Putin. Yet his actions are much tougher than Obama's. Remember, Obama defended Putin when Romney criticized him. Joe Biden said Putin was an ally. And they also, Obama refused to send lethal weapons to Ukraine. Well, President Trump has given Ukraine lethal weapons to use against the Russians. We've killed hundreds of Russian fighters in Syria. that's the country that obama invited the russian dental so again i it is disconnect and president uh... trumpet is a criticism of him he cannot accept the fact that russia metal because of his mind that puts a cloud over his election victory and to me he's got to get off that he's hurting the country and he's hurting our intelligence community uh... his own man i mean uh... dan colts was a conservative republican senator and he's head of the uh... national television agency and do you 