    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "You know, we've tried this for 70 years. I mean, you go back to Eisenhower and Khrushchev and Kennedy and Khrushchev and Really, the only ones who really worked was Reagan when he firmed up our policy and called the Soviet Union evil empire and stood firm. I think the Russians understand us being firm. You know, we could, virtual wanted to, we get a good relationship tomorrow. I mean, if they just were more cooperative, they weren't trying to interfere in our elections, if they weren't constantly, again, the aggression in Ukraine, their movements in the Middle East. So, you know, the Russians are big boys. No one has to be nice of them. If they know that any time they want to have good relations with us, the US is going to be available to do that. The US will do that. Now, listen, with all of this, we can still find areas of agreement, not because we like each other. I mean, during the high of the Cold War, we had some common cause with Russia, some common cause with China. I mean, that's part of diplomacy. But that doesn't mean that you say they're good guys. And probably what bothered me the most is when the president said there's enough blame on both sides. To me, there's no equivalence between the United States and Russia. There's no equivalence. Again, I think critical of President Obama. I don't question his patriotism. I don't, and I certainly don't blame him for the bad relations we have with Russia. That's all because of Russia. President, going back to President Bush, he did all he could to have solid relations with Russia, and we found out then that we couldn't trust him. President Obama comes in, they have the reset button, they wanted to work with Obama. with Putin during the first four years, President Obama did all he could to work with him, even told after I'm elected that I can make a better deal with you, that's I think. And again, Putin just went into Georgia, went into Ukraine, he's momentum trouble around the world. So to me, this is all on Russian side, not on ours. They know we're available if this is going to be honest negotiations.",
